ource-located diagnostics and no Roslyn runtime dependency in consumer.\n- [x] Actual compiler consumer plus invalid/generic/inaccessible/duplicate/partial/namespace diagnostics tested.\n- [x] Peer semantic-symbol collision fixed and exact original5repros independently rejected.\n\nOriginal CLI/scaffolding/transport-schema acceptance remains unchecked, original W5 milestone and #11 dependency remain intact. No new tracking card was created.\n\n## Evidence and limits\nEngine umbrella maturity remainsM0; actual person-hours remainnull. Retained failures include source-isolation warnings, Unicode/cancellation corrections, generator display-name collision and Invalid first benchmark. Canonical NuGet source is isolated to official nuget.org;13new build-time graph packages have actual hash/license metadata, not redistribution/security approval. No public/NuGet release or billing changes.\n\n- [W1 delivery report](https://github.com/Cephalon-Labs/Cehpalon-Engine-Docs/blob/main/internal/planning/w1-core-composition-codegen.md)\n- [Exact-source evidence](https://github.com/Cephalon-Labs/Cehpalon-Engine-Docs/blob/main/internal/evidence/w1/delivery-manifest.json)\n- [Predeclared protocol](https://github.com/Cephalon-Labs/Cehpalon-Engine-Docs/blob/main/internal/validation/w1-component-protocol.md)\n- [Hosted CI blocker](https://github.com/Cephalon-Labs/Cehpalon-Engine-Docs/blob/main/internal/evidence/w1/hosted-ci.json)\n\n\n## Portable CLI/scaffold subset — 2026-10-29\nBefore: registration generation only. After: one experimental source-checkout portable-request-reply console scaffold with actual Core/Composition/generated dispatch, plus strict pure configuration validation. Selected by agents from current Project 4 (23 items, zero Ready) under user authorization to continue portable work while #3 stays Blocked. This is a bounded subset of this existing card; original W5, dependencies #2/#11, native Type, labels, priority, estimate40–80h/midpoint60, null actual/remaining hours and M0 remain unchanged. Full acceptance checkboxes and full Test/Benchmark Planned remain unchanged.\n\n- [x] Source-only CLI new/validate/help/version; strict supported profile/arguments, fixed9files, observed17input hash manifest and explicit analyzer-only code generation reference. No shell/build/install/download/services by CLI.\n- [x] Actual generated console consumer compiles configuration before activation, lazily registers typed handlers, dispatches shared business code and disposes owned handler/modules. Main on/off/invalid cases prove zero disabled/invalid activation; this public Core example has no tenant authority.\n- [x] No overwrite or merge; deterministic source bytes, owned fixed-file stage cleanup, injected write/publication failures, competing destination preservation, observed link/device/metacharacter checks and real checkout boundaries.\n- [x] Exact clean final Engine component suites: Windows462/0failed (Tooling115), Linux459/0failed (Tooling112), actual SDK compiler fixture passed. Three Windows-only alias tests explain the count difference.\n- [x] Actual CLI process + fresh generated consumer restore/locked-restore/build/run:70checks per local host sequentially, Unicode/space/ampersand source clone paths, on/off/invalid config, actual emitted registry, compiler-free runtime graph and8collision-name consumers. Runtime graph is consumer/Core/Composition only.\n- [x] Hosted component CI40754466014 passed462/459 and compiler fixture at final Engine revision; downloaded source hashes independently match committed Git blobs. Hosted platform CI40754466002 passed12/0failed/2Not run per OS. CLI-generated E2E itself ran locally, not hosted.\n\nRetained failures: five tiny compiler repros, Windows integration02 System assembly MissingMethodException, and intermediate hosted CI40753720357's exactly one nested-runner-wrapper Tooling failure per host. Namespace/assembly prefixes and actual Git-marker boundary recognition correct these; final complete matr