      "local": "<!-- cehpalon-task: tooling -->\n## Outcome\nBuild CLI, scaffolding and operation-contract code generation\n\n## Scope and acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Generate minimal selected profiles and compatible transport schemas\n- [ ] Fail on unsupported combinations with actionable diagnostics\n- [ ] Validate generated consumers build and E2E behavior matches selected features\n\n## Tracking\n- Type: Feature (native issue type)\n- Labels: area:tooling\n- Priority: P2 (Project field)\n- Milestone: W5 - Tooling and Distribution\n- Owner: Cephalon-Neza\n- Dependencies: #2, #11\n- Parent: None; acceptance checklist defines the initial work breakdown.\n- Feature/function: tooling\n- Estimated person-hours: 40–80 (low confidence; planning midpoint 60)\n- Estimate assumptions: first bounded capability slice, including relevant implementation, tests and docs; refine after architecture/provider choices. Not universal provider coverage or a delivery-date promise.\n- Actual person-hours: null (not measured; do not infer from AI or CI duration)\n- Remaining estimate: null (not yet refined)\n- Maturity before / observed: M0; runtime/provider/version/host proof not established\n- Maturity target: define per supported capability/profile before implementation\n\n## Validation\n- Test required: Yes; task-appropriate review/metadata/link checks for documents, contract/E2E/failure checks for runtime.\n- Test result: Exact-clean components509Windows/506Linux and actual compiler fixture passed at both new revisions. Full generated SmallAPI133+39HTTPS, export160+25differential and portable70perhost belong to Candidate01; Candidate02 changes only recorder options and repeats components/all benchmark generated-consumer checks. Independent raw replay28,758/30,009checks passed. Full task gates remain Planned; current CI is step-free infrastructure Blocked.\n- Benchmark: Both complete original-protocol candidates executed and retained; correctness passed, performance Observed/not_qualified. Variance goal NOT achieved: final generator7Windows/4Linuxunstable groups; Windows export-off CV16.638835% and mean346.8358ms exceed baseline15.220958%/320.0426ms. Do not select the favorable middle result. Full Benchmark qualification remains Planned.\n- Evidence: add immutable Engine revision, locked dependencies, commands, results and proof limits when run.\n\n## References\n- [Program plan](https://github.com/Cephalon-Labs/Cehpalon-Engine-Docs/blob/main/internal/planning/2026-10-27-program-plan.md)\n- [Delivery and maturity](https://github.com/Cephalon-Labs/Cehpalon-Engine-Docs/blob/main/internal/standards/delivery-and-maturity.md)\n- [Task mirror](https://github.com/Cephalon-Labs/Cehpalon-Engine-Docs/blob/main/tasks/20.md)\n\n## Engine commit journal\n- `55c630fc5d4c47258a1a2b0da4a16ce8bc42b9f7` - reuse compact journal options only; complete Candidate02 correctness passed, variance goal unresolved, all negative observations retained.\n- `1b9d538b4311cf574912596a0f547ae5ae788070` - generator work/allocation reduction and cold serving/GraphQL source split; semantic regressions/full generated consumers passed, complete Candidate01 variance mixed/regressed.\n- `29df762cf28d12bd0d587b3c9d99925bcb99b14f` - fixed observational generator/emit benchmark, solution/locked build/source inventory and CI path coverage; complete local matrix, no runtime library change or qualification promotion.\n- 972522eb455d0b1b6415cf4e88398c14baa82fbe - offline Small API serializer-derived OpenAPI/actual GraphQL SDL export, shared typed catalog, pure HTTP schema helper and bounded contracts; full gates remain open.\n- 535e6be86428a135da1b4abd8399ab9bd299a8bf - Small API CLI/scaffolding with actual HTTPS/JWT/generated tenant gateways, optional GraphQL and lifecycle/configuration contracts; full gates remain open.\n- 39ae0cc6ae56045a9d3d24f94eb564efa5941254 - distinguish actual Git checkout roots from same-named hosted runner wrappers, preserving allowed .local output and real checkout protection.\n- b921a6d1cde5ec5d138d8efe84b760d6241de461 - avoid generated consumer compiler/framework/Engine namespace and assembly collisions; final exact-revision proof below includes the complete collision-name corpus.\n- 3974c7d8099945e4446e210e04bca2ab630f3174 — experimental portable CLI; full gates remain open.\n- `fee491cecaba04232207a1a2884057498e81213e` — portable Core, strict Composition/lifecycle, incremental typed operation registry, tests/consumer fixture and bounded benchmark runner; full platform/feature gates remain explicit.\n\n## Change history\n- 2026-10-27: Created from the user-authorized new baseline and all three selected sample lanes. Historical task IDs and test results were not imported.\n\n## W1 portable development refinement — 2026-10-27\nUser authorized Core/Composition development and operation code generation while #3 remains Blocked. Existing dependencies and full acceptance gates remain unchanged. Portable local implementation/tests may proceed with the pinned private SDK; this is not supported-Windows qualification, a hosted-CI pass, or release authorization.\n\nUser requested code generation now: implement the bounded operation-registration incremental generator as support for W1. Full CLI/scaffolding/transport-schema and real transport E2E remain under this existing W5 task and its original #11 dependency. Do not mark those delivered by registration generation alone.\n\n- [Portable development ADR](https://github.com/Cephalon-Labs/Cehpalon-Engine-Docs/blob/main/internal/adr/ADR-0005-w1-portable-core-composition.md)\n- [Code-generation ADR](https://github.com/Cephalon-Labs/Cehpalon-Engine-Docs/blob/main/internal/adr/ADR-0006-incremental-operation-code-generation.md)\n- [Predeclared protocol](https://github.com/Cephalon-Labs/Cehpalon-Engine-Docs/blob/main/internal/validation/w1-component-protocol.md)\n\n## Early generator subset delivered — 2026-10-27\n- [x] Incremental typed/lazy operation registry generated at build time, with source-located diagnostics and no Roslyn runtime dependency in consumer.\n- [x] Actual compiler consumer plus invalid/generic/inaccessible/duplicate/partial/namespace diagnostics tested.\n- [x] Peer semantic-symbol collision fixed and exact original5repros independently rejected.\n\nOriginal CLI/scaffolding/transport-schema acceptance remains unchecked, original W5 milestone and #11 dependency remain intact. No new tracking card was created.\n\n## Evidence and limits\nEngine umbrella maturity remainsM0; actual person-hours remainnull. Retained failures include source-isolation warnings, Unicode/cancellation corrections, generator display-name collision and Invalid first benchmark. Canonical NuGet source is isolated to official nuget.org;13new build-time graph packages have actual hash/license metadata, not redistribution/security approval. No public/NuGet release or billing changes.\n\n- [W1 delivery report](https://github.com/Cephalon-Labs/Cehpalon-Engine-Docs/blob/main/internal/planning/w1-core-composition-codegen.md)\n- [Exact-source evidence](https://github.com/Cephalon-Labs/Cehpalon-Engine-Docs/blob/main/internal/evidence/w1/delivery-manifest.json)\n- [Predeclared protocol](https://github.com/Cephalon-Labs/Cehpalon-Engine-Docs/blob/main/internal/validation/w1-component-protocol.md)\n- [Hosted CI blocker](https://github.com/Cephalon-Labs/Cehpalon-Engine-Docs/blob/main/internal/evidence/w1/hosted-ci.json)\n\n\n## Portable CLI/scaffold subset — 2026-10-29\nBefore: registration generation only. After: one experimental source-checkout portable-request-reply console scaffold with actual Core/Composition/generated dispatch, plus strict pure configuration validation. Selected by agents from current Project 4 (23 items, zero Ready) under user authorization to continue portable work while #3 stays Blocked. This is a bounded subset of this existing card; original W5, dependencies #2/#11, native Type, labels, priority, estimate40–80h/midpoint60, null actual/remaining hours