cks (HTTP51; Tooling151/148), actual compiler fixture; three Windows-only alias tests explain counts. New helper checks include nullable/nested/recursive shape, detached ownership, four parallel workers, actual error/null response serialization.\n- [x] Complete generated export proof160harnesschecks +25actualruntime differential checks per host sequentially: four configs twice, exact artifact sets/hashes, real SDL AST equality, actual routes/HTTPS DTO/error bodies, schema-valid id0 rejected by custom validation, cross-tenant denials and forbidden GraphQL exposure still rejected. Owned readonly-parent failure proves provider/schema/disposal1 with no host/dispatch/output; permissions restored.\n- [x] Complete prior Small API proof repeated at the same Engine revision:133harnesschecks +39HTTPS cases per host, externally configured serving/tenant/disabled/cleanup; portable regression70checks per host including8collision-name consumers. No old W0 performance workload substitution.\n\nOpenAPI covers only three business operation routes, not health or GraphQL HTTP envelopes. Schemas are structural and do not encode every numeric parser bound, duplicate/UTF8/body-size rule, validation lambda or tenant policy. JSON-schema proof interpreter intentionally supports emitted fixture keywords only, not universal validator certification. No performance/provider/production/AOT/distribution acceptance or arbitrary endpoint/schema generation is claimed. Timing benchmark Not required for this bounded artifact-correctness slice; full #20 tooling benchmark remains Planned.\n\nNew component CI40838078446/platform40838078343 were rejected before execution:4jobs/0steps and explicit payment/spending-limit annotations. This is Blocked infrastructure, not current CI pass or code failure; no forced unchanged rerun or billing action. #3 body/editable metadata remain identical/Blocked. Original #9 full Test/Benchmark Blocked and #20 In Progress/P2/full gates Planned, W5/#2/#11 dependencies, Type/labels/estimates/null hours/M0 remain unchanged.\n\nRetain all integration/final attempts and the first recursive-record test fixture compile failure (copy-constructor conflict), corrected without weakening runtime checks. Raw schemas/source/logs exclude credentials/private fixtures, artifacts and clone objects; observed source hashes are not immutable full-build attestation and trusted-parent/race limits remain.\n\n- [Decision ADR0014](https://github.com/Cephalon-Labs/Cehpalon-Engine-Docs/blob/main/internal/adr/ADR-0014-small-api-contract-export.md)\n- [Predeclared correctness protocol](https://github.com/Cephalon-Labs/Cehpalon-Engine-Docs/blob/main/internal/validation/tooling-contract-export-protocol.md)\n- [Delivery report](https://github.com/Cephalon-Labs/Cehpalon-Engine-Docs/blob/main/internal/planning/tooling-contract-export.md)\n- [Exact-source results](https://github.com/Cephalon-Labs/Cehpalon-Engine-Docs/blob/main/internal/evidence/tooling-contracts/delivery.json)\n- [Actual artifact/runtime differential proof](https://github.com/Cephalon-Labs/Cehpalon-Engine-Samples/tree/main/tooling-contracts)\n\n\n## Tooling observations - 2026-10-30\nUser continued existing #20 after offline contract export. Before: source-only CLI/scaffold/export correctness, no fixed current tooling measurement matrix. After: actual Roslyn DriverRun+PEEmit versus independently authored equivalent typed registry PEEmit, plus real CLI new/validate/four selected offline export fresh processes. Runtime libraries/templates unchanged; Core/Composition/codegen and actual emitted consumers are exercised. Full acceptance remains open; W5/#2/#11 dependencies, In Progress/P2/M0, full Test/Benchmark Planned, Type/labels/estimates and null hours unchanged. #3 body/editable metadata stays identical and Blocked.\n\n- [x] Predeclared sizes1/3/32 x fresh/no-op/edit, independent registration AST and lazy-factory/dispatch/disposal parity, exact two paired primers then five paired repetitions of three. P